hi there Steve Kaufman here again to  talk about language learning online and  in particular to talk about the online  language teacher I think this is a  rapidly growing phenomenon more and more  independent teachers of many different  languages are either setting up their  own shop whereby they teach online via  Skype or similar you know video exchange  systems but Skype is probably the most  popular so these people either are  independent or they are involved in  websites that group these teachers and  offer them to learners such as I talked  to you which is the one that I have used  and you know while we offer native  language tutoring at linked in many  languages we don't have tutors and and I  think that we need to do a better job  with how we offer the opportunity for  our our members to interact with native  speaking tutors but leaving that aside  it recently in Polish in Ukrainian in  Greek now I have gone to high talkie so  I want to talk a little bit about the  experience my experience I have also  taught English via Skype what do I think  are the prerequisites or the ideal  conditions or how should the online  language teacher best help the learner  now I talk of course from my perspective  the way I like to learn so I think what  are the goals of the online language  teacher to me I think the number one  objective is to be encouraging to the  learner that's the absolute most  important thing because most of the  learning is not done during the lesson  most of the learning is done outside the  lesson reading or listening or otherwise  trying to engage with people in the  language remember it's your attitude and  it's the time you spend that's going to  determine your success in language  learning so if the teacher the online  language teacher can encourage create a  positive attitude  make the learner want to come back to  you as a teacher or make the learner  want to spend more time with the  language that's the number one goal to  encourage the learner the second most  important goal is to give the learner a  chance to speak because we have ample  opportunity to listen I have I less than  an hour a day while doing other chores  washing dishes driving a car that's  resizing and I can read but I don't have  much opportunity to speak some teachers  think that it's their job to do a lot of  speaking I think that is not so useful  so a good online language teacher has to  know how to bring out the learner what  is the learner interested in let the you  know ask the learner questions to  encourage the learner to speak and the  teacher should not speak very much I  don't think that the hour or half an  hour that we have online with the native  speaker is there in order to teach the  grammar or teach the vocabulary because  a lot of that however much you explain  or teach is gonna be forgotten anyway of  course you can add so the teacher should  answer any questions that the learner  has but I think the main goal should be  to engage the learner and have the  learner speak the target language I'm  also not a great fan of reading along or  role-playing for example recently I had  my Greek tutor say okay today we're  gonna do role-playing and she sent me a  sort of a series of words having to do  with what you say at the airport and  passport show me your documents baggage  and so forth and so on and she started  she sent me this and said have a look at  that have a look at this and then so  where are your documents were gonna  pretend you're going through customs I  said no thank you I'm not gonna do that  I want to talk about things that are  meaningful to me in fact I'm not now  going through customs so I don't want it  10 that I'm going through customs I  would like to talk about things that are  interesting and I have lots of things  I'm interested in and I'm sure we can  find lots of topics to discuss so fine  he had no problem with that so we  reverted back to our conversation mode  after our discussion and this is another  important point she the tutor writes all  of my mistakes down either immediately  into a Google document which you know I  can see online if I want to follow along  and she's writing these things down  which is something useful because if the  tutor introduces new vocabulary I can  never understand anything when I hear it  the first time if I read it I at least  understand what she's saying or hear it  better because I can read it but then I  get this list of my words and phrases  afterwards and then I review them in  link now given whether you're in link or  not the accessibility of online  dictionaries means to me at least you  don't have to put the English or the  translation into this this just here are  the words and phrases you have trouble  with I get the report and I study it so  then I looked at her list of things that  one says at the airport related to  checking in and and going through  security and sovereigns on so I went  through it and I of course had to erase  all the English then I imported it into  link and studied it and I thought to  myself this is useful information it  would be even better if she could record  it which I told her and she said yeah  that'd be great I can do that and that's  it occurred to me to that even better  with this information if she could make  some kind of repetitive story or even a  bunch of sentences where the vocabulary  repeats and she records it this again  gives me an opportunity to review this  content reading and then listening more  than once especially if the vocabulary  repeats so again the idea here is that  the to her the online tutor is someone  who should be encouraging the learner to  learn maybe providing learning  content that the learner can review  afterwards ideally with with a recorded  voice so this can have this can be for  example items of specific vocabulary as  in the case of the airport or if it's  issues of grammar again maybe the online  tutor can create some sample sentences  sentences where if it's a verb the same  ideas are expressed in different tenses  or different persons you know with  recording so then the learner can go off  and work on this material all of this  then leads to the idea that the exchange  with the online tutor is this  opportunity for the learner to speak for  the learner to get stimulated it becomes  certainly in my case sort of a milestone  I want to improve for my next engagement  for me  typically three four times a week an  hour each time is ample in fact if it  weren't for the fact that I'm going to  creep in you know a month and a half  from now I would speak even less because  I find that I have to engage with with  the language through reading and  listening and and then if I have a few  opportunities a week to to speak you  know that serves the purpose I don't  think you learn just through speaking at  a later stage when I'm better of course  I eventually need to speak a lot but if  you speak three four hours a day online  with the online tutor that can become  quite expensive I am hoping that I'll  reach a level where when I'm in Crete  and this is maybe a bit unrealistic I  can sit around with some locals drink a  bit of yuzu and speak Greek for three  four hours that would be really  meaningful this is what I was able to do  when I went to Prague for my Czech or  that I went to l'viv for my Ukrainian  and I was getting had the opportunity  for a lot of face to face conversation  and there you really develop  that fluency through using the language  a lot the difficulty on Skype is that  it's you know you're paying for an hour  or whatever it is the connection often  is not ideal so it's more difficult to  clearly hear what the person is saying  so so I think I think the I online tutor  therefore has to be realistic in terms  of what can be achieved aim at  encouraging for example if the online  tutor doesn't quite hear what the  learner is saying or if the learner  totally mispronounces a word or doesn't  say the word correctly the worst thing  the online tutor can do is sort of go  huh you know and I get that sometimes  sorry I didn't say it correctly  instead the tutor has to find some way  of indicating that he or she didn't  understand and try to get the learner to  say it again or if he or she can't make  an effort to try to understand what the  person is saying from the context and  start to use some of that vocabulary  because to summarize them number one  goal is to encourage the learner so that  the learner leaves the online lesson  more motivated to learn not less and  second of all to get that person to  speak and then however badly the person  did or thinks they did to then encourage  them and tell them how well they did  again with the intention of getting them  to spend more time with the language and  come back again so there you have a a  quick rant on the role of the online  language tutor if you like these videos  please subscribe bye for now  [Music]
 

